Backport of upstream permaweb/HyperBEAM 04b7b2b7 ("Optimize codec ID generation
hot paths", 2026-06-23, 262 commits past v0.9-FINAL), reduced to the minimal fix.

message_to_ordered_list/2 eagerly evaluated erlang:hd(SortedKeys) to pass as the
pivot argument. For an emptied or meta-only map (e.g. a committed empty map
#{<<"commitments">> => ...}) SortedKeys is [] -> hd([]) -> badarg. That crashed
dev_lua:decode after any compute that leaves a Lua state map empty (removing its
last key), 400ing the push AND corrupting the slot checkpoint -> the process
wedges permanently (all subsequent reads 500). Fixed upstream on edge/v1.0; this
guards the empty case so the map decodes to [] instead of crashing.

See anyone-protocol docs/hyperbeam-migration/UPSTREAM-ISSUES.md (A15).

